  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "Epic three‑set with monster Other One > Eyes jam and sunshine vibes",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a towering Other One into Eyes of the World that rolls into a delicate China Doll, while Here Comes Sunshine lifts the second set. Jerry’s new ‘Wolf’ guitar tone shines and Phil’s booming bass underpins the jams. The three‑set marathon is captured in full on the recommended SBD.",
    "review": "May 13, 1973 at the Des Moines State Fairgrounds finds the Dead deep in a creative stride. Set 1 rolls through classics – a tight China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and a heartfelt “Don’t Ease Me In” into “Around & Around”. The second set builds momentum with “Here Comes Sunshine” and a propulsive “Playing In The Band”, setting the stage for a monumental third set. After “He’s Gone” and “Truckin’”, Bill Kreutzmann drives an expansive drum break that launches into a monster “The Other One”. Jerry’s guitar soars, especially on his new Wolf‑tone licks, before the band flows seamlessly into “Eyes Of The World”, where Keith Godchaux’s Tyner‑style piano adds richness. The sequence resolves with the haunting “China Doll” and a rousing encore of “Casey Jones”. Across all five soundboard sources the performance is consistently praised – the only real complaint being occasional hiss on the full‑show tape. The standout moments, tight rhythm section, and crystalline partial releases make this one of 1973’s essential recordings.",
